      <CodeBlock code={"2015-05-01T19:48:36.300593110Z time=\"2015-05-01T19:48:36Z\" level=info msg=\"version=v2.0.0+unknown\"\n2015-05-01T19:48:36.303294724Z time=\"2015-05-01T19:48:36Z\" level=info msg=\"redis not configured\" instance.id=9ed6c43d-23ee-453f-9a4b-031fea646002\n2015-05-01T19:48:36.303422845Z time=\"2015-05-01T19:48:36Z\" level=info msg=\"using inmemory layerinfo cache\" instance.id=9ed6c43d-23ee-453f-9a4b-031fea646002\n2015-05-01T19:48:36.303433991Z time=\"2015-05-01T19:48:36Z\" level=info msg=\"Using OpenShift Auth handler\"\n2015-05-01T19:48:36.303439084Z time=\"2015-05-01T19:48:36Z\" level=info msg=\"listening on :5000\" instance.id=9ed6c43d-23ee-453f-9a4b-031fea646002"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="registry-accessing-metrics_accessing-the-registry" class="group scroll-mt-20">Accessing registry metrics<a href="#registry-accessing-metrics_accessing-the-registry" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">The OpenShift Container Registry provides an endpoint for <a href="https://prometheus.io/docs/introduction/overview/">Prometheus metrics</a>. Prometheus is a stand-alone, open source systems monitoring and alerting toolkit. The metrics get exposed at the <em><strong>/extensions/v2/metrics</strong></em> path of the registry endpoint. You can access the metrics by running a metrics query that includes a cluster role.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create a cluster role if you do not already have one to access the metrics:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ cat <<EOF | oc create -f -\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: ClusterRole\nmetadata:\n  name: prometheus-scraper\nrules:\n- apiGroups:\n  - image.openshift.io\n  resources:\n  - registry/metrics\n  verbs:\n  - get\nEOF"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Add the cluster role to a user account by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc adm policy add-cluster-role-to-user prometheus-scraper <username>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      For the metrics query, get the user token.
      <CodeBlock code={"openshift:\n$ oc whoami -t"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Run a metrics query in node or inside a pod. The following example command and output demonstrate this task.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ curl --insecure -s -u <user>:<secret> \\ (1)\n    https://image-registry.openshift-image-registry.svc:5000/extensions/v2/metrics | grep imageregistry | head -n 20"} lang="terminal" />
      <ul>
